1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,317
Today is September 20, 2026.

3
00:00:07,317 --> 00:00:18,040
Overnight, the S&P 500 closed up 12.74 points, or 0.17 percent, after dipping to 7610 intraday.

4
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:23,628
The Nasdaq added 104 points, gaining 0.39 percent.

5
00:00:23,628 --> 00:00:28,395
Volume spiked on Triple Witching Day, the third Friday of September.

6
00:00:28,395 --> 00:00:34,253
Stock options, futures, and index options all expired simultaneously.

7
00:00:34,253 --> 00:00:38,285
That inflates volume but does not shift the underlying trend.

8
00:00:38,285 --> 00:00:41,300
The real story this week was the Fed.

9
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:46,826
The central bank hiked rates, and the hawkish tone triggered a sharp selloff on Wednesday.

10
00:00:46,826 --> 00:00:49,437
But here is the critical nuance.

11
00:00:49,437 --> 00:00:53,456
This was the smallest rate increase in roughly fifty years.

12
00:00:53,456 --> 00:00:58,052
The dot plot shows one more hike this year and at most one next year.

13
00:00:58,052 --> 00:01:01,704
That is a cumulative seventy-five basis points.

14
00:01:01,704 --> 00:01:04,621
The policy toolbox is running thin.

15
00:01:04,621 --> 00:01:10,111
Every rate-hike cycle since the 1980s has produced a positive S&P return.

16
00:01:10,111 --> 00:01:14,106
The market is not in a 2022-style bear setup.

17
00:01:14,106 --> 00:01:17,978
Ten-year Treasury yields have broken above five percent.

18
00:01:17,978 --> 00:01:21,116
August bond inflows hit a record high.

19
00:01:21,116 --> 00:01:23,775
The allocation math is simple.

20
00:01:23,775 --> 00:01:26,937
Lock in a five percent yield for a decade.

21
00:01:26,937 --> 00:01:28,824
That is compelling.

22
00:01:28,824 --> 00:01:31,312
But the bears are not silent.

23
00:01:31,312 --> 00:01:36,324
Bank of America strategists are flagging a path to five percent on the two-year.

24
00:01:36,324 --> 00:01:43,076
Rate swaps are pricing three more hikes into the 4.50 to 4.75 range.

25
00:01:43,076 --> 00:01:48,125
BofA is bearish on the two-year, expecting the yield to push through five.

26
00:01:48,125 --> 00:01:50,344
The divergence is real.

27
00:01:50,344 --> 00:01:53,652
The consensus says tightening is nearly over.

28
00:01:53,652 --> 00:01:56,226
The risk case says it is not.

29
00:01:56,226 --> 00:02:01,201
After two days of digestion, the hawkish overhang has largely cleared.

30
00:02:01,201 --> 00:02:04,277
The market has absorbed the tightening shock.

31
00:02:04,277 --> 00:02:08,616
The dominant narrative is rotating back to artificial intelligence.

32
00:02:08,616 --> 00:02:15,062
On the geopolitical front, the US and China are expected to hold a summit in Washington next week.

33
00:02:15,062 --> 00:02:19,351
Trump is reportedly planning to meet the Chinese president at the airport.

34
00:02:19,351 --> 00:02:22,905
That breaks standard American diplomatic protocol.

35
00:02:22,905 --> 00:02:25,074
The signal is deliberate.

36
00:02:25,074 --> 00:02:29,486
A trade truce extension past October is the headline prize.

37
00:02:29,486 --> 00:02:35,442
A one-year extension, or even a full-term deal, would be a major positive for equities.

38
00:02:35,442 --> 00:02:41,005
AI safety coordination between the two powers is a secondary but meaningful outcome.

39
00:02:41,005 --> 00:02:43,836
The core risk is not a new tariff.

40
00:02:43,836 --> 00:02:47,746
The core risk is a sudden, unilateral escalation.

41
00:02:47,746 --> 00:02:51,851
As long as that does not happen, the macro floor holds.

42
00:02:51,851 --> 00:02:55,895
Now let us connect that liquidity picture to the tech complex.

43
00:02:55,895 --> 00:03:02,133
The Philadelphia Semiconductor Index gapped down early this week on AI safety concerns.

44
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:09,780
A coalition of nearly a hundred researchers from Stanford, Johns Hopkins, and nonprofit labs published an open letter.

45
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:15,466
They are demanding third-party safety audits with deep access to frontier model internals.

46
00:03:15,466 --> 00:03:18,273
That scare hit the semi tape hard.

47
00:03:18,273 --> 00:03:21,643
But by Friday, the gap was fully filled.

48
00:03:21,643 --> 00:03:25,062
Twenty-six of thirty components closed higher.

49
00:03:25,062 --> 00:03:27,206
Only four were red.

50
00:03:27,206 --> 00:03:31,189
The index has effectively bottomed and is entering a rebound.

51
00:03:31,189 --> 00:03:35,062
The pure memory and storage names are leading the recovery.

52
00:03:35,062 --> 00:03:39,706
When that segment turns, the broader index finds its next leg up.

53
00:03:39,706 --> 00:03:42,513
Capital is rotating with conviction.

54
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:46,643
Berkshire Hathaway completed its leadership transition this week.

55
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:49,559
Warren Buffett stepped down as chairman.

56
00:03:49,559 --> 00:03:56,140
His son Howard is now non-executive chairman, focused on agriculture and food security research.

57
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:58,959
But the real operator is Greg Abel.

58
00:03:58,959 --> 00:04:05,037
He holds full operational and capital allocation authority over a multi-hundred-billion-dollar book.

59
00:04:05,037 --> 00:04:08,211
And Abel has started deploying into AI.

60
00:04:08,211 --> 00:04:12,868
He is buying Google, both in the open market and through a private placement.

61
00:04:12,868 --> 00:04:14,755
That is a signal.

62
00:04:14,755 --> 00:04:19,976
The largest value investor in the world is tilting toward the AI capex cycle.

63
00:04:19,976 --> 00:04:24,020
The HBM supply chain is the tightest link right now.

64
00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:28,640
Long-term supply agreements have locked in pricing for the next two years.

65
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:33,983
Any capacity expansion converts directly into revenue and margin expansion.

66
00:04:33,983 --> 00:04:38,260
That is why the memory names are the most active in the entire market.

67
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:41,974
Let us go deep on the three names that matter most today.

68
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:44,284
Micron Technology.

69
00:04:44,234 --> 00:04:46,783
Earnings land at the end of the month.

70
00:04:46,783 --> 00:04:51,514
The street is modeling earnings per share up roughly ten times year over year.

71
00:04:51,514 --> 00:04:53,634
That is not a typo.

72
00:04:53,634 --> 00:04:55,386
Ten times.

73
00:04:55,386 --> 00:04:59,112
The HBM contract book is fully allocated.

74
00:04:59,112 --> 00:05:02,445
Long-term agreements have fixed the price floor.

75
00:05:02,445 --> 00:05:06,024
Capacity additions flow straight to the bottom line.

76
00:05:06,024 --> 00:05:09,345
The stock has reclaimed the thousand-dollar level.

77
00:05:09,345 --> 00:05:11,636
And here is the key point.

78
00:05:11,636 --> 00:05:14,332
The valuation has not stretched.

79
00:05:14,332 --> 00:05:18,609
A ten-fold earnings expansion has fully absorbed the price gain.

80
00:05:18,609 --> 00:05:23,046
Micron is the single most traded name in the market by dollar volume.

81
00:05:23,046 --> 00:05:26,698
Institutional flow is concentrated and aggressive.

82
00:05:26,698 --> 00:05:28,818
The risk is cyclical.

83
00:05:28,818 --> 00:05:31,759
Memory pricing is not a straight line.

84
00:05:31,759 --> 00:05:36,318
A future price correction could pull the stock back toward its starting point.

85
00:05:36,318 --> 00:05:40,680
But right now, this is the strongest momentum name in semis.

86
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:44,247
Support sits just below the thousand-dollar mark.

87
00:05:44,247 --> 00:05:48,144
A close below that invalidates the short-term thesis.

88
00:05:48,144 --> 00:05:49,823
Netflix.

89
00:05:49,823 --> 00:05:53,180
Wells Fargo just cut the rating to Underweight.

90
00:05:53,180 --> 00:05:57,078
The target price dropped from eighty dollars to fifty-seven.

91
00:05:57,078 --> 00:05:59,774
That is a twenty-eight percent haircut.

92
00:05:59,774 --> 00:06:02,984
The logic is structural, not cyclical.

93
00:06:02,984 --> 00:06:07,494
Viewing hours are declining as users fragment across platforms.

94
00:06:07,494 --> 00:06:13,193
User growth hit a ceiling roughly two years ago, and the company stopped reporting the metric.

95
00:06:13,193 --> 00:06:16,207
There is no connection to the AI trade.

96
00:06:16,207 --> 00:06:21,293
AI-generated short-form content is actually cannibalizing screen time.

97
00:06:21,293 --> 00:06:23,904
The hit franchises are wrapped.

98
00:06:23,904 --> 00:06:26,232
Stranger Things is over.

99
00:06:26,232 --> 00:06:28,389
Squid Game is over.

100
00:06:28,389 --> 00:06:30,497
The pipeline is thin.

101
00:06:30,497 --> 00:06:36,060
If a streamer cannot sustain high growth, the market reclassifies it as a utility.

102
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:39,749
And Netflix does not pay a utility-grade dividend.

103
00:06:39,749 --> 00:06:42,139
The capital has a better home.

104
00:06:42,139 --> 00:06:45,080
The streaming crown remains intact.

105
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:48,205
But the growth premium is being stripped away.

106
00:06:48,205 --> 00:06:52,690
Any bounce from here is a mean-reversion trade, not a trend trade.

107
00:06:52,690 --> 00:06:54,124
Tesla.

108
00:06:54,124 --> 00:06:57,090
No major catalyst in the near term.

109
00:06:57,090 --> 00:07:01,318
The stock is grinding higher in a slow, orderly uptrend.

110
00:07:01,318 --> 00:07:05,031
The gap from the last earnings print has been fully filled.

111
00:07:05,031 --> 00:07:11,269
Without a new product announcement or a policy tailwind, Tesla will simply track the broader index.

112
00:07:11,269 --> 00:07:14,381
There is no independent alpha here right now.

113
00:07:14,381 --> 00:07:17,090
It is a hold, not a chase.

114
00:07:17,090 --> 00:07:19,749
One final note on positioning.

115
00:07:19,749 --> 00:07:22,053
Qualcomm is the outlier.

116
00:07:22,053 --> 00:07:26,759
It fell more than five percent on Friday, directly against the sector.

117
00:07:26,759 --> 00:07:29,933
The Philadelphia Semi Index gapped up.

118
00:07:29,933 --> 00:07:32,163
Qualcomm gapped down.

119
00:07:32,163 --> 00:07:34,590
That divergence is a warning.

120
00:07:34,590 --> 00:07:40,693
If the semi rebound continues, Qualcomm either catches up or it is being sold for a reason.

121
00:07:40,693 --> 00:07:43,609
Watch the next two sessions closely.

122
00:07:43,609 --> 00:07:47,617
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

123
00:07:47,617 --> 00:07:51,783
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
